SUMMARY:Native Plant Walk: Pollinators and Plant Morphology
DESCRIPTION:Have you ever wondered which native plants attract which pollinators\, or are you hoping to welcome specific pollinators to your garden? \nJoin staff from the Library of North Carolina’s Government and Heritage Library and the NC Museum of Natural Sciences for a Native Plant Walk focusing on the connections between native plants\, pollinators\, and plant morphology. \nThis plant walk will explore native plantings in the NC Department of Natural and Cultural Resources’ Native Plant Meadow and the NC Museum of Natural Science’s Native Plant Garden. The event will take place primarily outdoors\, with participants traveling approximately ½ mile round-trip via paved sidewalks. \nRegister Here \nThis event is hosted in connection with the GHL’s Native Plant Seed Library. Learn more about our seed library at https://slnc.info/seeds.
URL:https://www.naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/plant_walk_morphology/
LOCATION:Archives\, History\, & State Library Building\, 109 East Jones\, Raleigh\, North Carolina\, 27601
CATEGORIES:Adults,Outdoor Experiences,Special Events
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://www.naturalsciences.org/calendar/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/July-Plant-Walk.png
ORGANIZER;CN="Valerie%20MacNabb":MAILTO:valerie.macnabb@naturalsciences.org
END:VEVENT
