SUMMARY:Nature Play Day at NCMA
DESCRIPTION:*This program takes place at the North Carolina Museum of Art. Please meet us near the Welcome Center. *  \nCome out and play! We will be stocking part of the outdoor park with extra-special materials and supplies to encourage nature exploration and outdoor play! A Prairie Ridge play facilitator will be present to help you play your way. Supplies may vary each month\, but may include fun things like fort-building equipment\, puppets and costumes\, bubbles\, paint\, and more.  \nThis is a free\, drop-in program. Staff and supplies will be available from 10:00 am – 12:00 pm. This program is completely outdoors\, so come dressed for the weather and ready to potentially get messy! Designed for ages 7 & younger – everyone welcome! 
URL:https://www.naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/nature-play-day-at-ncma/
LOCATION:North Carolina Museum of Art\, 2110 Blue Ridge Rd\, Raleigh\, 27607
CATEGORIES:Children,Nature Play Days,Outdoor Experiences,Walk-up Programs
ORGANIZER;CN="Kiersten%20Bowser":MAILTO:kiersten.bowser@naturalsciences.org
END:VEVENT
